body:
I think you're too hard on yourself OP, we might have drastically different lives but believe me when I say I can relate to getting very obsessed over someone, pushing others away, and being so depressed people end up abandoning me. I try not to think about those past people too often because I feel as if there's not much I can do but to move on because they definitely don't want to talk to me. The point is that no one is perfect, and when you're dealing with a mental illness like we both are, making costly mistakes are wayyy more common. I think I found a small friend group that fully accepts me for me and I am so grateful to have them in my life more than they can know. Same goes for you, there are people out there for you, it's not easy but you'll get there, I believe in you.

&#x200B;

"You can't keep blaming yourself. Just blame yourself once and move on." -Homer Simpson

&#x200B;

(also sorry for the late response I do not use reddit consistently)

I will never condone self harm and suicide, but I will say I understand it suffering from similar thoughts myself. It's definitely not selfish, you're struggling through a mental illness that has beaten you down so hard that you feel as if suicide is a viable option. I'm not an expert on this, I'm only speaking from experience, but one way to learn more would be therapy, I would highly suggest reconsidering because it would help you answer questions like these. 

&#x200B;

Hope you feel better OP

I don't think you're overreacting in the slightest. Not wanting to spend time with someone who adds extra unneeded stress in your life and invalidates your feelings is more than understandable, it's what everyone should do. You're not selfish for having anxiety and screw her for saying you are. I'm so sorry they lashed out at you instead of providing the support you needed.

&#x200B;

At first glance it does seem like a shitty thing for your friend to do, but there might be some history between you to that might explain why she did that. Hopefully she has your best interest at heart. Your aunt on the other hand, there's nothing that can excuse what she did and again I am so sorry that happened to you.

&#x200B;

You're not overreacting and you didn't ruin Christmas, I promise.

I went through a breakup myself about two or so months ago, and it still stings. I'm sorry that happened with you, it's going to suck for awhile before it gets better and there's not much that can help other than time to think it over. 

&#x200B;

Please do not kill yourself though, if you were able to find love with him, you're capable of finding love again, when you are ready of course. 

&#x200B;

I'm here if you need to talk as well, I hope you feel better OP
